 Persian 𐏋 (XŠ /⁠xšāyaθiya⁠/, “king”). Doublet of Check, Schah, and Scheck.\nOriental words were usually borrowed into Middle High German through Italian or Old French. Therefore the final /x/ is remarkable, because this sound was replaced with /k/ in Italian scacco, Old French échec. There are two possible explanations for this: Either the word was borrowed directly from Arabic during the early Crusades, or it was borrowed through Middle Dutch schaec and the -ch goes back to artificial reproduction of the High German consonant shift (as happened in several other words).",{"g":"n:m","decl":"|||s|s|s|s|s","alt":[["n","|||s|s|s|s|s"],["m",""]]}]],"senses":[[15287,"schach","noun","chess (game)",0,"n"],[15288,"schach","noun","check (chess situation in which the king is directly threatened)",1,"n"],[15289,"schach","noun","obsolete form of Schah (“Persian or, by extension, other Oriental ruler”)",2,"m",["obsolete"]],[15290,"schach","noun","obsolete form of König (“chess king”)",3,"m",["obsolete"]]],"related_forms":[[21981,"schach","blindschach","derived"],[21982,"schach","blitzschach","derived"],[21983,"schach","damenschach","derived"],[21984,"schach","dauerschach","derived"],[21985,"schach","doppelschach","derived"],[21986,"schach","reiseschach","derived"],[21987,"schach","schachanleitung","derived"],[21988,"schach","schachaufgabe","derived"],[21989,"schach","schachbrett","derived"],[21990,"schach","schachbuch","derived"],[21991,"schach","schachclub","derived"],[21992,"schach","schachfibel","derived"],[21993,"schach","schachfigur","derived"],[21994,"schach","schachgebot","derived"],[21995,"schach","schachgenie","derived"],[21996,"schach","schachgroßmeister","derived"],[21997,"schach","schachklub","derived"],[21998,"schach","schachländerkampf","derived"],[21999,"schach","schachmannschaft","derived"],[22000,"schach","schachmatt","derived"],[22001,"schach","schachmeister","derived"],[22002,"schach","schachmeisterschaft","derived"],[22003,"schach","schacholympiade","derived"